            "buttonSize": "big",
            "goToSlideType": "specified",
            "invisible": false,
            "solution": ""
          },
          {
            "x": 2.23463687150838,
            "y": 13.245033112582783,
            "width": 92.73743016759778,
            "height": 86.09271523178808,
            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><strong>Early Life of Siddhartha Gautama</strong><br>\nSiddhartha Gautama, who would become known as the Buddha, was born into a royal family in present-day Nepal. His father, King Suddhodana, wished for his son to be a great king and shielded him from the suffering of the world. Despite the comfort of palace life, Siddhartha was moved by the suffering he encountered on rare trips outside the palace walls.</p>\n\n<p><strong>The Four Sights</strong><br>\nOn these journeys beyond his palace, Siddhartha encountered \"the four sights\" that would change his perspective on life. He saw an old man, a sick man, a dead body, and a monk. These sights taught him about aging, sickness, death, and the possibility of finding peace away from worldly possessions and pain.</p>\n\n<p><strong>The Great Renunciation</strong><br>\nDetermined to understand the meaning of suffering, Siddhartha abandoned his royal life and family at the age of 29. This event is known as the Great Renunciation. He began a journey of ascetic life, depriving himself of worldly comforts in search of enlightenment. His trials included rigorous fasting and meditation practices.</p>\n"
              },
              "metadata": {
                "contentType": "Text",
                "license": "U",
                "title": "Unbenannt: Text",
                "defaultLanguage": "en"
              },
              "subContentId": "53bc5361-5ce5-43a9-a00f-57bbceee9cd0"
            },
            "alwaysDisplayComments": false,
            "backgroundOpacity": 0,
            "displayAsButton": false,
            "buttonSize": "big",
            "goToSlideType": "specified",
            "invisible": false,
            "solution": ""
          }
