          {
            "x": 2.178649237472767,
            "y": 12.910611231371064,
            "width": 92.73743016759778,
            "height": 86.09271523178808,
            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><strong>Spreading the Teachings</strong><br>\nFor the next 45 years, the Buddha traveled through the northern regions of India, teaching his path to enlightenment to a diverse range of people. His teachings attracted a large following and were characterized by the use of simple language so that everyone could understand and benefit from them.</p>\n\n<p><strong>The Sangha</strong><br>\nThe Buddha established a monastic community known as the Sangha. This community was made up of monks, nuns, and laypeople who supported each other in the practice of the Buddha's teachings. The Sangha played a crucial role in preserving and spreading his teachings after his death.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Final Days</strong><br>\nThe Buddha passed away at the age of 80 in Kushinagar, India. His last words were a reminder to his followers to work diligently on their spiritual path. His death was not the end but a passing into Nirvana, which in Buddhism means the end of suffering and the cycle of death and rebirth.</p>\n"
              },
              "metadata": {
                "contentType": "Text",
                "license": "U",
                "title": "Unbenannt: Text",
                "defaultLanguage": "en"
              },
